    {
      "id": "stdlib.statistics-median-grouped-quantiles-correlation-covariance-linear-regression",
      "category": "stdlib",
      "feature": "statistics.median_grouped / quantiles / correlation / covariance / linear_regression",
      "status": "partial",
      "tests": [
        "42_statistics_paired"
      ],
      "reject_tests": [
        "rejects/statistics_quantiles_keyword"
      ],
      "note": "median_grouped follows the CPython 3.13 formulation: it finds the value at the midpoint, counts the points at or below it, then interpolates across the class interval. The older 'nudge the two central values' algorithm disagrees whenever the median value is repeated. quantiles implements CPython's exact integer rescaling (j = i*m//n, delta = i*m - j*n), which deliberately extrapolates outside the observed range. correlation, covariance, and linear_regression validate pair length, minimum sample size, and constant input."
    },
    {
